{
 "source": "hand-written: the action scheduler's queue (mock_server_scheduler_queued_tasks, Scheduler.getQueue().size()) holds the forward continuations waiting for the action thread a semantic drift analysis holds (actionHandlerThreadCount 1); they are not delayed tasks, so mock_server_pending_delayed_tasks stays 0",
 "peer": true,
 "properties": {
  "metricsEnabled": "true",
  "actionHandlerThreadCount": "1",
  "llmProvider": "OPENAI",
  "llmBaseUrl": "{{peerurl}}",
  "llmApiKey": "test-key",
  "llmModel": "gpt-test",
  "llmRequestTimeoutMillis": "40000",
  "driftSemanticAnalysisEnabled": "true"
 },
 "steps": [
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/reset",
   "node": "peer"
  },
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/expectation",
   "node": "peer",
   "body": [
    {
     "id": "classify",
     "httpRequest": {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/v1/chat/completions"
     },
     "httpResponse": {
      "statusCode": 200,
      "headers": {
       "content-type": [
        "application/json"
       ]
      },
      "body": "{\"id\": \"chatcmpl-1\", \"object\": \"chat.completion\", \"model\": \"gpt-test\", \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"message\": {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"1|BREAKING|The status changed.\"}, \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}], \"usage\": {\"prompt_tokens\": 10, \"completion_tokens\": 5, \"total_tokens\": 15}}",
      "delay": {
       "timeUnit": "MILLISECONDS",
       "value": 30000
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "upstream",
     "httpRequest": {
      "path": "/thing"
     },
     "httpResponse": {
      "statusCode": 500
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/expectation",
   "body": [
    {
     "id": "stub",
     "httpRequest": {
      "path": "/thing"
     },
     "httpResponse": {
      "statusCode": 200
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "method": "PUT",
   "path": "/mockserver/expectation",
   "body": "[{\"id\": \"forward\", \"priority\": 10, \"httpRequest\": {\"path\": \"/thing\"}, \"httpForward\": {\"host\": \"{{peerhost}}\", \"port\": {{peerport}}}}]",
   "mask": [
    {
     "regex": "\"host\" : \"[^\"]*\"",
     "replace": "\"host\" : \"<peer>\""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "note": "nothing queued yet",
   "method": "GET",
   "path": "/mockserver/metrics",
   "mask": [
    {
     "regex": "(?m)^(?!(?:# (?:HELP|TYPE) )?mock_server_(?:scheduler_queued_tasks|pending_delayed_tasks))[^\\n]*\\n",
     "replace": "",
     "reason": "only the series this scenario drives; the rest are pinned by metrics.json"
    },
    "content-length: \\d+"
   ]
  },
  {
   "note": "its semantic analysis holds the only action thread (actionHandlerThreadCount 1) for 20 s (longer here so all 30 forwards arrive while it holds the thread, even on a loaded machine). The backend answers after 30 s, but the client's read timeout, maxSocketTimeout (20 s by default), ends the call first (and before llmRequestTimeoutMillis does), so it fails, nothing is cached, and each later analysis waits 20 s for the backend again (a 20 s backend raced the read timeout, and won in the 9.1.0 recording)",
   "method": "GET",
   "path": "/thing"
  },
  {
   "sleepMillis": 500
  },
  {
   "async": "f0",
   "maxMillis": 45000,
   "method": "GET",
   "path": "/thing",
   "note": "30 forwards at once: each one's continuation waits for the thread, first come first served; once it is free, each continuation submits its analysis behind the remaining continuations, so the first 16 fill the backlog (max(16, 4 x 1 thread)) and the other 14 are shed"
  },
